WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.210
JENNY BROWN: Today we're talking
about Domains, Databricks,

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.490
VMware Engine, and budgets.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.950
I'm Jenny and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.610
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.220
We're introducing Cloud
Domains in preview,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.190
which simplifies domain
registration and management

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.870
within Google Cloud.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.660
Cloud Domains improves the
custom domain experience

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.180
for developers,
increases security,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.010
and supports
stronger integrations

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.530
around DNS and SSL.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.260
It offers easy domain
renewal through Cloud Billing

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.270
and permissions via IM.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.240
Check out the release
for more information.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.970
By deploying on Google
Cloud, Databricks users

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.600
can build data lakes fast and
integrate data science and ML

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.390
workloads on their path
towards production.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.600
Databricks capabilities in
data engineering and analytics

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.020
are complemented by Google
Cloud's global secure network.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.110
And all together, customers
get an enterprise-ready cloud

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.240
service with a
Databricks experience

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.660
that's reliable, scalable,
secure, and governed.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.870
Read more about this
integration on the blog.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.870
Google Cloud VMware Engine
simplifies the challenges

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.240
of moving and modernizing
critical workloads

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.380
to the cloud.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.680
To make networking simpler and
enhance security management,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.050
we've recently released
improved networking,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.170
support, scalability, and
support for the VMware

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:22.840
platform, and improved
reach, among other things.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.380
Check out the blog
for the full list.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.690
Budgets and alerts are
probably the first step

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.390
to staying on top of
your Google Cloud costs.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.730
If you care about money,
you should definitely

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.900
set up a budget.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.660
Check out the blog post Mark
Mirchandani to learn more.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.810
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.550
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.040
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.610
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.750
We'll see you in the cloud.

